Hi Michael,

Following our discussion yesterday, the plan brings the twelve intake intents=
 together as one classification problem, with 0.82 macro-F1 as the first-year=
 research target. It is a target, not a result. Readers will work from the re=
ceived body and establish a supported answer through independent reading and =
adjudication; the destination and later handling are not evidence of the send=
er's intent.

I've attached the issued plan, MDR-STI-20240416-RP-01-R01. Please feel free t=
o circulate it to the research team. Brandon and I will handle the conditions=
 for use separately; meeting the research target alone would not settle that =
decision.

Thanks,
Vanessa

On April 10, 2024 at 10:18 AM, Michael Serrano wrote:
> Hi Vanessa,
>
> For Monday at 2:00, could you sketch what we should allow a reader to see i=
n a short intake message and how we would establish a defensible correct answ=
er? I would like us to distinguish the request in the text from the destinati=
on or subsequent handling of the message.
>
> Please bring options for the number of intent categories and a first-year t=
arget; let's decide those together at the meeting. Separately, list the infor=
mation we would need before deciding whether a result is suitable for use. A =
research score alone will not settle that question.
